module
public import Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30RunEnvelopes
/-!
# Mixtures of single black cells with gaps of at least ten and double black cells with gaps of at least eight

**Partial result.** For every nonempty list of blocks `(r, q)` with `r = 1` and `q ≥ 10`, or `r = 2` and
`q ≥ 8`, chosen independently, the single-seed center column is not eventually the repeating word
`1^(r₁) 0^(q₁) … 1^(rₖ) 0^(qₖ)`, whatever the transient (`not_eventually_asymmetric_mixtures`). The
number of blocks, their order and the gaps are unbounded. `Rule30IsolatedMixtures` is the case `r = 1`
everywhere; `Rule30WhiteRunEight` gives the single word `1 1 0^q` for `q ≥ 8`.

In the ten-cell strip relaxation, either kind of block moves every strip set through four nested
envelopes `A0 ⊇ A1 ⊇ A2 ⊇ A3 ⊇ A4` (`1024 → 221 → 162 → 137 → 128` strips; `stage0`–`stage4`), each
closed under white steps, so the shortest allowed gap suffices (`Rule30RunEnvelopes.pump_capture`).
`A4` is closed under every allowed block. From `A4`, column `1` along a white run reads `0 0 1 …` after
one black cell and `1 …` after two, so `orCol 0` is eventually periodic, which masked Jen forbids
(`Rule30RunEnvelopes.no_word_of_invariant`). All finite checks are `decide +kernel`.
-/
@[expose] public section
set_option Elab.async false
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0
